01:32.780 --> 01:36.940
-Brazil- São Paulo

01:38.980 --> 01:42.820
This will be my last passing practice with Roberto.

01:43.580 --> 01:46.370
You played very well yesterday.

01:47.420 --> 01:49.180
Thanks!

02:08.460 --> 02:12.820
I'm glad I ended my stint in Brazil with a win.

02:12.820 --> 02:16.420
So, did you decide where you're going next?

02:17.900 --> 02:21.340
All the teams in Europe are offering great deals for you.

02:21.340 --> 02:25.660
The Brancos are letting you make the final decision.

02:25.660 --> 02:27.190
I haven't decided yet,

02:27.910 --> 02:30.700
but I'm thinking about going to Spain first.

02:30.700 --> 02:33.820
I want to go there in person and let my feet decide.

02:33.820 --> 02:35.500
I see.

02:37.250 --> 02:38.700
Roberto.

02:39.290 --> 02:42.700
Thank you for everything you've done for me!

02:45.110 --> 02:46.860
Tsubasa...

02:48.390 --> 02:51.710
Soar onto the global stage from here.

02:54.980 --> 03:00.140
<b>New Stage of Dreams</b>

02:54.980 --> 03:00.140
<b>New Stage of Dreams</b>

03:00.590 --> 03:04.040
The Champions Tournament will decide the number one team in Europe.

03:04.040 --> 03:06.780
Two Japanese players stand on this stage of dreams.

03:07.320 --> 03:11.600
The soccer kid who advanced to Europe after playing in Japan and Brazil,

03:11.600 --> 03:13.020
Ohzora Tsubasa,

03:13.810 --> 03:16.900
and the super great goalkeeper,

03:16.900 --> 03:19.100
Wakabayashi Genzo.

03:19.100 --> 03:21.060
It's a Clash of the Titans!

03:22.600 --> 03:24.500
Here I come, Wakabayashi-kun!

03:24.500 --> 03:26.100
Come, Tsubasa!

03:26.100 --> 03:27.430
Go, Tsubasa!

03:27.430 --> 03:29.100
Stop it, Wakabayashi!

03:32.940 --> 03:35.070
Sir, sir?

03:35.940 --> 03:37.460
Sir?

03:37.970 --> 03:41.910
The plane is about to land. Please fasten your seat belt.

03:41.910 --> 03:43.460
Okay.

03:44.030 --> 03:45.250
So, it was a dream, eh?

03:46.330 --> 03:50.780
But if Wakabayashi-kun and I
 could have a Japanese duel

03:50.780 --> 03:54.890
in the Champions Tournament's final that decides the best in Europe,

03:54.890 --> 03:57.780
it would surely be fun.

03:58.420 --> 04:02.540
In Europe, I'll improve into a player who won't lose to the best teams in the world.

04:03.550 --> 04:07.540
I'll definitely become the best player in the world!

04:21.950 --> 04:24.500
Become masculine like Hyuga!

04:24.500 --> 04:26.260
Scrubbing Face Wash Tiger Shot.

04:26.260 --> 04:29.060
Win a Hyuga Kojiro T-shirt!

04:29.710 --> 04:32.370
Hyuga-kun sure is a star athlete now.

04:35.910 --> 04:37.690
Hello, Nakazawa speaking.

04:37.690 --> 04:38.600
Hello?

04:38.600 --> 04:39.540
Tsubasa-kun?

04:39.540 --> 04:43.270
Yeah, I just arrived in Barcelona, Spain.

04:43.270 --> 04:44.470
Barcelona?

04:44.470 --> 04:45.470
Yeah.

04:45.470 --> 04:48.580
I'm going to check out Europe on my own from here.

04:48.580 --> 04:51.480
I see... Europe.

04:51.480 --> 04:53.540
How's it going with you, Sanae-chan?

04:53.540 --> 04:54.930
I'm doing well.

04:54.930 --> 04:57.630
Ishizaki-kun and the others are playing hard in the J-League.

04:57.630 --> 04:59.990
The only thing that's changed here...

04:59.990 --> 05:04.450
Oh, right! Hyuga-kun is transferring to the Italian League!

05:05.780 --> 05:10.460
Hyuga-kun's transfer is all the buzz among Japanese soccer fans!

05:10.460 --> 05:14.730
Italian League / FC Piemonte Transfer Press Conference {TS:  What font should be used for this line?}{koku: I say let TheDeath handle it, lol}

05:14.730 --> 05:19.220
Hyuga Kojiro  / Italian League / FC Piemonte Transfer Press Conference {TS:  What font should be used for this line?}{koku: I say let TheDeath handle it, lol}

05:19.220 --> 05:21.200
It's her.

05:21.200 --> 05:23.620
Hyuga's skillful agent.

05:23.620 --> 05:25.620
She's notorious for getting commercials,

05:25.620 --> 05:31.310
magazine features, and major sponsors for him.

05:31.310 --> 05:33.060
That's not all.

05:33.060 --> 05:39.280
She's also credited for the fast transfer of Hyuga to the Italian League.

05:39.280 --> 05:45.020
Is it really true that she wrapped up the negotiations in the blink of an eye?

05:45.020 --> 05:50.000
Yeah, she even planned a short exchange program with an Italian school,

05:50.000 --> 05:53.340
and demonstrated Hyuga's skills to their scouts.

05:53.340 --> 06:01.070
Then after they returned, she went through negotiations before the buzz dissipated in Italy.

06:01.070 --> 06:03.830
That's what makes her a great strategist.

06:08.800 --> 06:10.480
It's almost time.

06:11.810 --> 06:15.950
Hyuga-kun, this is your first step toward the world stage.

06:15.950 --> 06:16.860
Matsumoto-san.

06:16.860 --> 06:17.340
Eh?

06:17.340 --> 06:19.720
I really appreciate what you've done for me.

06:19.720 --> 06:22.060
You're the one who recruited me to Toho Academy,

06:22.060 --> 06:24.860
and you got me the opportunity to transfer to Piemonte so quickly.

06:24.860 --> 06:26.620
It's all thanks to you.

06:26.620 --> 06:29.320
You don't have to thank me.

06:29.320 --> 06:30.820
Be confident in yourself.

06:30.820 --> 06:35.100
You earned the Piemonte transfer with your own skills.

06:35.630 --> 06:36.970
Matsumoto-san...

06:37.620 --> 06:42.060
Also, I advanced further in my career thanks to you.

06:42.060 --> 06:45.640
I'm glad I quit Toho Academy's scouting department.

06:45.640 --> 06:49.540
Today, I'm the female president of my own management agency.

06:49.990 --> 06:51.830
Let's get going.

06:51.830 --> 06:52.540
Okay.

06:52.540 --> 06:56.710
But even if Hyuga is a top player in Japan,

06:56.710 --> 06:58.540
I wonder if he'll be effective in Italy.

06:58.540 --> 07:00.120
You're probably right.

07:00.120 --> 07:04.700
The Italian League is famous for its Catenaccio defensive style of soccer.

07:04.700 --> 07:06.020
"Catenaccio?"

07:06.020 --> 07:09.700
It means "door-bolt," which protects the gate.

07:09.700 --> 07:15.340
Goals are usually defended by the "gatekeeper."  In other words, by the goalie himself.

07:15.770 --> 07:17.580
But it's different in Italy.

07:17.580 --> 07:21.340
The entire team functions as the "catenaccio" and protects the goal.

07:21.340 --> 07:26.670
A striker like Hyuga actually picked such a defensive league on purpose?

07:26.670 --> 07:28.830
I guess so.

07:29.600 --> 07:30.380
They're here.

07:34.340 --> 07:44.980
Hyuga Kojiro  / Italian League / FC Piemonte Transfer Press Conference{+TS0509} {TLC/TS:  Seems like a long sign for such a short name.}{koku: same sign as before}

07:36.580 --> 07:42.840
I would like to thank the members of the press for gathering here today.

07:42.840 --> 07:48.540
Hyuga Kojiro will now explain his decision to transfer to the Italian League.

07:49.620 --> 07:52.830
My dream is to become the best striker in the world.

07:52.830 --> 07:55.770
I am going to Italy to fulfill that dream.

07:56.370 --> 07:59.340
To the Italian League, the league known for the greatest defenses in the world.

07:59.340 --> 08:01.380
To break those defenses? No.

08:01.380 --> 08:03.780
To destroy them!

08:04.260 --> 08:06.780
I'm transferring to Piemonte!

08:06.780 --> 08:10.010
My goal is to become the leading goal scorer in the Italian League!

08:12.480 --> 08:13.580
I see.

08:13.580 --> 08:16.130
Hyuga-kun is going to Piemonte in the Italian League.

08:16.980 --> 08:19.150
Good luck to you, too, Tsubasa-kun!

08:19.150 --> 08:19.670
Thanks.

08:19.670 --> 08:24.950
I'll cheer for you no matter where you go, as Tsubasa's number one fan!

08:24.950 --> 08:26.180
Thanks.

08:26.180 --> 08:27.980
I'll let you know when I decide where to transfer.

08:28.640 --> 08:29.560
Yeah.

08:29.980 --> 08:31.840
Okay, later.

08:33.950 --> 08:36.000
Hyuga-kun is going to Italy, huh?

08:36.000 --> 08:37.970
All right, I'm picking my team, too!

08:49.620 --> 08:52.580
It's that uniform...

09:01.100 --> 09:03.540
Hey, buddy! Want a ride in the taxi?

09:03.540 --> 09:05.300
Y-Yeah!

09:09.850 --> 09:11.550
That billboard poster...

09:11.550 --> 09:12.780
Oh, that's Rivaul.

09:12.780 --> 09:15.180
I want to get to his team's home stadium.

09:15.180 --> 09:17.320
Sure, I'll take you there.

09:18.210 --> 09:22.100
This is Gaudí's famous Sagrada Família.

09:22.100 --> 09:23.420
Uh, um...

09:23.420 --> 09:25.620
Want to see the Columbus Monument next?

09:25.620 --> 09:27.950
I'm trying to get to...

09:29.340 --> 09:31.160
I know, I know.

09:31.160 --> 09:33.340
This guided tour is just a little bonus.

09:44.020 --> 09:49.340
Have fun, buddy! This is the largest soccer stadium in Europe,

09:49.340 --> 09:51.820
Cataluña Stadium!

09:54.000 --> 09:56.340
Cataluña Stadium, huh?

09:57.510 --> 10:01.910
What? Tsubasa Ohzora of Brancos came for a visit?

10:02.740 --> 10:05.860
Welcome, Tsubasa Ohzora.

10:06.460 --> 10:11.270
Your performance with the Brancos is also highly acclaimed here in Spain.

10:11.270 --> 10:14.170
As the Club's chairman, we are very fortunate that you came when I'm here.

10:14.170 --> 10:16.980
That way, I can show you around the stadium.

10:16.980 --> 10:18.900
Thank you very much.

10:20.660 --> 10:26.460
Our club won the Spanish League Championship title this season.

10:26.460 --> 10:31.350
We have maintained our honor as a team using this stadium as our home field.

10:31.350 --> 10:32.080
Um...

10:32.080 --> 10:32.660
Yes?

10:32.660 --> 10:36.420
Can you let me stand on the pitch?

10:36.830 --> 10:40.010
Please do! This way.

11:18.590 --> 11:21.430
It's that stadium I saw in my dream!

11:25.490 --> 11:30.140
This is the greatest tourist attraction in Barcelona for soccer fans.

11:30.580 --> 11:34.700
The Cataluña Stadium, with a maximum capacity of 120,000!

11:34.700 --> 11:39.620
This is where the super star, Rivaul, plays!

11:39.620 --> 11:42.900
Hey, Pinto! You sneaked in again?

11:42.900 --> 11:44.900
Wait, kid!

11:44.900 --> 11:45.850
Hold it!

11:47.560 --> 11:48.340
My ball!

11:49.550 --> 11:50.860
I've decided!

11:51.480 --> 11:52.570
What did you just say?!

11:56.860 --> 11:58.940
I've decided to play here!

12:21.840 --> 12:24.500
The ball is your friend. Take good care of it!

12:24.500 --> 12:26.340
Who are you?

12:26.340 --> 12:30.340
I'm Tsubasa.  I've transferred here from the Brancos in Brazil.

12:30.340 --> 12:33.180
Cataluña's Ohzora Tsubasa!

12:33.980 --> 12:35.830
Ohzora Tsubasa...

12:37.130 --> 12:38.580
So cool!

12:51.320 --> 12:53.070
Tsubasa!

12:53.900 --> 12:55.660
Wait!

12:59.250 --> 13:00.780
Could you give me your autograph, Tsubasa?

13:00.780 --> 13:01.660
You're the boy from earlier...

13:01.660 --> 13:05.080
You kicked the ball back to me, right?

13:05.080 --> 13:06.760
That was so cool!

13:06.760 --> 13:08.660
I became your fan!

13:08.660 --> 13:10.350
Thanks.

13:10.350 --> 13:13.860
Then you're my first new fan after my transfer.

13:13.860 --> 13:14.660
What's your name?

13:14.660 --> 13:17.020
I'm Pinto!

13:17.020 --> 13:18.860
So, you're Pinto.

13:18.860 --> 13:20.060
Nice to meet you.

13:22.060 --> 13:24.540
<b>O
h
z
o
r
a
 
T
s
u
b
a
s
a</b>

13:25.190 --> 13:25.970
Thank you.

13:25.970 --> 13:28.810
I've been a fan of this team ever since I was born.

13:28.810 --> 13:31.310
You can ask me if you need anything.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.280
Really?

13:32.280 --> 13:35.090
Then I want to see the team practicing.

13:35.090 --> 13:37.060
Can you tell me where they practice?

13:37.060 --> 13:38.890
Of course!

13:38.890 --> 13:42.580
But the top team is playing an away game today.

13:42.580 --> 13:47.330
The B-team and the youth team are practicing in the fields over there.

13:47.330 --> 13:49.460
Would you like to see the practice fields, too?

13:50.200 --> 13:51.980
Yes, I would love that.

13:51.980 --> 13:55.580
This way.  Hurry up!  Hurry up!

14:02.060 --> 14:07.380
Cataluña Practice Fields

14:02.380 --> 14:05.070
Wow, there are so many players practicing.

14:05.070 --> 14:07.580
They're players from Cataluña's B-team.

14:07.580 --> 14:11.580
It's Cataluña's farm team, playing in the second division.

14:12.710 --> 14:16.590
The B-team players' dream is to play in the first division,

14:16.590 --> 14:22.240
but they have to prove their skills and get promoted into the top team.

14:35.100 --> 14:37.330
Are you all right? Get yourself together.

14:38.720 --> 14:41.140
What's going on here, Gonzalez?

14:41.140 --> 14:43.680
He just took a hit from Almieja.

14:43.680 --> 14:46.750
He challenged us after we said, "Anyone who can score a goal on us

14:46.750 --> 14:52.140
will get a recommendation from the three of us to Coach Edward in the top team."

14:53.010 --> 14:55.610
Come on! Someone try to beat us!

14:56.320 --> 14:58.800
It's your chance to be promoted to the top team!

15:00.290 --> 15:02.160
All right, I'll do it!

15:02.870 --> 15:04.660
It's Serrano, B-team's leading goal scorer!

15:07.350 --> 15:09.900
Good, come at us however you want.

15:10.360 --> 15:11.570
You don't need to hold anything back.

15:11.570 --> 15:13.080
Just try to get past us!

15:16.660 --> 15:17.860
Here I come!

15:20.860 --> 15:22.420
Let me get this guy, too!

15:29.940 --> 15:31.940
Good, I got past him!

15:33.180 --> 15:33.980
It's not over yet!

15:33.980 --> 15:36.340
I was going after this from the start!

15:48.380 --> 15:50.500
They are defenders from the top team,

15:51.020 --> 15:52.380
Gonzalez,

15:53.380 --> 15:54.660
Clemente,

15:55.500 --> 15:56.820
and Almieja.

15:57.100 --> 16:00.460
They were in rehab from injuries,

16:00.460 --> 16:02.980
but it looks like they're all better now!

16:02.980 --> 16:05.250
I'm really looking forward to our next season.

16:06.020 --> 16:08.760
What's wrong? No one else?

16:09.830 --> 16:12.830
It's impossible to get past three defenders from the top team!

16:12.830 --> 16:15.300
We'll just get injured trying!

16:15.790 --> 16:16.980
I'll do it!

16:18.220 --> 16:19.480
Tsubasa!

16:20.440 --> 16:22.580
Let me try!

16:23.040 --> 16:24.400
Who the hell are you?

16:24.400 --> 16:25.720
We don't have time for spectators!

16:26.240 --> 16:28.260
He's not a spectator.

16:28.260 --> 16:30.400
He's joining our team starting next season.

16:30.400 --> 16:31.580
He's Tsubasa Ohzora.

16:32.120 --> 16:33.420
What?

16:34.650 --> 16:38.370
Serrano, let him borrow your cleats.

16:38.370 --> 16:39.510
Yes, sir! {kk: "ah"= yes}

16:40.590 --> 16:42.680
Tsubasa Ohzora...

16:42.680 --> 16:44.280
That guy from Brancos?!

16:45.050 --> 16:47.500
The top team's starting lineup is already full.

16:47.500 --> 16:51.500
If he's joining, then one of us would be cut.

16:52.400 --> 16:55.660
Looks like a formidable opponent just showed up.

16:56.110 --> 16:59.890
Even if these cleats are borrowed, this body is mine.

16:59.890 --> 17:01.170
I will always fight on.

17:01.830 --> 17:03.200
The three-against-one battle...

17:04.680 --> 17:06.660
No, it's three-on-three!

17:08.090 --> 17:11.500
The ball and the pitch are always my friends!

17:11.500 --> 17:13.560
Why are you grinning?

17:13.560 --> 17:15.220
Bring it on!

17:15.220 --> 17:16.460
Okay!

17:16.920 --> 17:17.980
It's a serious match!

17:20.030 --> 17:20.740
Here I come!

17:21.980 --> 17:25.510
Come, kid! This is your entry test!

17:25.510 --> 17:29.500
We'll test you to see if you're fit to join Cataluña!

17:29.920 --> 17:32.980
This is a battlefield, and the fight has already begun!

17:33.390 --> 17:35.540
I'll go first!

17:38.640 --> 17:40.660
His form is flawless!

17:41.050 --> 17:42.580
But I'm still getting past you!

17:46.080 --> 17:46.860
Go!

17:46.860 --> 17:49.410
The Brazilian feint, huh?

17:49.410 --> 17:50.220
I won't let you past me!

17:52.740 --> 17:54.780
He's caught by Clemente's tight marking!

17:55.290 --> 17:57.780
Once he gets into that position, Clemente is unbeatable.

17:58.290 --> 18:00.450
He wraps his arms around just enough to avoid a foul,

18:00.450 --> 18:02.460
and contains his opponent.

18:02.460 --> 18:06.010
This is Clemente's Snake Marking!

18:07.380 --> 18:09.380
You can do it, Tsubasa!

18:09.980 --> 18:11.830
He's locked me down, and I can't move.

18:11.830 --> 18:15.060
So, this is Cataluña top team's defense.

18:16.520 --> 18:17.460
That guy...

18:18.160 --> 18:20.300
He's having an even match against Clemente!

18:20.300 --> 18:22.060
Amazing dribbling skills!

18:24.760 --> 18:27.620
He's not losing the ball even though I'm holding him down!

18:27.620 --> 18:29.100
Then you leave me no choice.

18:30.100 --> 18:31.050
Got it.

18:32.100 --> 18:33.340
His hold on my right side just weakened!

18:33.860 --> 18:34.680
All right!

18:36.740 --> 18:39.540
Yeah! He took advantage of his momentary weakness and got free!

18:41.080 --> 18:41.820
Take this!

18:41.820 --> 18:42.580
Watch out!

18:42.580 --> 18:44.580
He weakened his hold on purpose!

18:44.580 --> 18:48.820
How do you like the advanced defense by a European powerhouse team?!

18:50.060 --> 18:50.940
What?!

18:50.940 --> 18:51.860
He disappeared?

18:52.690 --> 18:53.940
H-He's above me!

18:53.940 --> 18:56.780
Sudden jump from that top speed?

18:56.780 --> 18:59.060
What incredible reflexes!

18:59.060 --> 19:00.190
Damn it...

19:00.190 --> 19:03.250
But my tackle has two stages!

19:03.900 --> 19:05.580
I've already seen that!

19:05.580 --> 19:07.020
What?

19:07.020 --> 19:08.980
Don't get carried away, kid!

19:09.680 --> 19:11.440
It never lets go of its prey,

19:11.440 --> 19:13.580
that's the top team's defense, too, huh?

